Z||000018||sjp777||05-20-2001||02:25 AM||||Jeez, bunch of tightwads.<P>The tool you can get from Rodney for $10 brand new.<P>The dew strips are $35 from any Pontiac dealer and if they don't have them in stock they can get them in 2 or 3 days.<P>Sure beats the cost of replacing door glass 'cause you waited to go the cheap route and now have scratches up and down the windows.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Nashco||05-20-2001||03:00 AM||||Tightwads?  I always thought that was called resourcefulness, or was it being economical?  Perhaps it was thrifty, I just can't seem to remember.  FYI, I ordered my dew strips from gmpartsdirect.com tonight, 55 bucks total including shipping.<P>The reasons to share the tool are pretty clear...we'll only need it once, and it doesn't make sense to buy a 12 dollar paper weight.  Doing it this way, it will cost me about 58 dollars (55 parts + 3 shipping for tool).  Going through Rodney and the dealership will cost you about 87 dollars (70 parts + 5 tax + 10 tool + 2 shipping).  So we can save almost 30 bucks by just being thoughtful and patient.<P>If my windows weren't already scratched by the previous owner, I would have done this a long time ago.  I just don't use the window unless necessary.  Unfortunately, I don't keep my money in the bank very well, so I can't afford to throw any of it around for no good reason.<P>Reduce, reuse, recycle....simple concept that could save us a lot of cash, time, and resources.  Anyway, have you ever noticed how simple Rodney's stuff is?  It's great for the beginner, but most of his stuff is just packaged thought.  I almost bought his dipstick shim at a whim when I got his headlight bushings.  After looking at it, I realized how stupid it would be to pay 4 dollars for a washer.  I used an electrical connector that I had cut off a wire, and fixed it for free.  I wish I had known what his headlight bushings were, I saw them at Lowe's the other night for 30 cents each.  (No offense to Rodney, I bought a shifter kit from him that I love, and wouldn't have had the ability to make on my own...he has good stuff)<P>Thought is easier than writing a check when you're in college <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||11
Z||000020||Topknot||05-20-2001||06:29 AM||||Hallo all,<P>Ok don't laugh but I am in need of some helpful advice to get my little 86 GT clutch up and running and to help out any other members also here's what I'll do.<P>I will BUY 10 drew strip tools from Rodney and freely give them out to any one who can assist me in getting my 86 GT V6 5 Speed clutch working!!!!!!!!<P>I am not wanting to drag the little car to a local shop being that 90 percent of them have no idea how to do it correctly or they won't even touch the Fiero.  I can do the work myself but need direction and pointers on going about it. <P>Yes I am spending night after coming home exausted from work reading, researching and trying to figure out what I need to do to work my problem out without having to drop the whole cradle.  being that the town I live in is not to big on cars torn apart laid out in ones front car port! hee hee.<P>So free dew tools for any help, then after your done using it pass it on and let others enjoy it's use.<P>Thanks Topknot =]<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||fropuff||05-20-2001||11:39 AM||||I agree..I am a tightwad.  I tend to find a cheap way to anything.  That way, you have money left over to do more projects, but you end up going the cheap way on those too!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I am only going to use the tool once, so I thought I'd be nice and let someone else take it.  Anybody else would do the same.  I'm not going the cheap way on the dew wipes.  I'm going to call the dealer tomorrow and order them.  When I was working at the dealer yesterday, I peeked into their GM parts book, and it says the dealer cost for the dew wipes are $19.00.  So $36 + tax + shipping.  I'm going to make sure that they're here by Friday.  I get more time than anyone else gets.  I have a three-day weekend to do them anyway.  Mail doesn't go on Memorial Day!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||10
