Z||000025||starfighter007@msn.com||05-24-2001||07:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Topknot:<BR><B>Hallo all,<P>Ok don't laugh but I am in need of some helpful advice to get my little 86 GT clutch up and running and to help out any other members also here's what I'll do.<P>I will BUY 10 drew strip tools from Rodney and freely give them out to any one who can assist me in getting my 86 GT V6 5 Speed clutch working!!!!!!!!<P>I am not wanting to drag the little car to a local shop being that 90 percent of them have no idea how to do it correctly or they won't even touch the Fiero.  I can do the work myself but need direction and pointers on going about it. <P>Yes I am spending night after coming home exausted from work reading, researching and trying to figure out what I need to do to work my problem out without having to drop the whole cradle.  being that the town I live in is not to big on cars torn apart laid out in ones front car port! hee hee.<P>So free dew tools for any help, then after your done using it pass it on and let others enjoy it's use.<P>Thanks Topknot =]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>                                                                                   well you do half to drop the cradle at least the rear portion  of the cradle.you need two jackstands a good floor jack you cacan take it all aprt your self no big deal,But you will need helpto put the tranny back in when you need to get the input shaft thru presure  plate and clutch disc. that is the hardest physycal part about the whole job.that part if every thing islined up perfectlyshoultake about 5to8 miniutesthen the rest of the job takeing your time doing every thing right should take know more than3maybe 4hours  takeingevry thing apart also should take about may 3 hours .Iam sure that there are hotdogs  out there that probly could do the whole job with air tools in about 3hours but just try to take your time and enjoy this time with your car I would also try tospread this job out over 2 days I hope this helps you a little. and thanks but kno thanks for the tool I want to wait my turn I think it willbe much more fun that way and remeber time is the essence to quality.goodluck Starfighter<BR>||||reg||1
