Z||000029||fropuff||05-31-2001||12:49 PM||||The tool was mailed to Monkeyman yesterday; it should be to him by Friday or Saturday.  It only takes a few hours to to the strips.  I started on the driver's side; took me about 45 minutes.  Very easy.  Then I moved to the passenger side; took 2 hours.  That was because the driver's side didn't have all the screw in.  I got mad at the passenger side, so I just cut the dew strip off the screws, then used the tool.  These can get pretty tight, and all the material moved away from it makes it a ton easier!  I also cheated when I put the screws back in.  I know I probably should have, but I didn't put the two screws in that you need the tool to take out.  I think there's three or four others than that, so I figured they'd hold it good.  As far as ordering some, don't go to the dealer!  They are a frickin ripoff!  At least mine was.  I figured they made a $45 profit on the two that I bought.  They cost $19.20 for the dealer to buy them, and $6 to two-day ship them.  At least I got em.  I think they make my car look a ton better!  Have a good one!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters rock!||||reg||1
Z||000030||tellron||05-31-2001||07:06 PM||||That dew wipe tool from Rodney works real well! I purchased my dew wipes from Suncoast Pontiac in Sarasota FL. The Suncoast Fiero Club has worked out a deal with the Parts Manager there to provide us with greatly reduced prices. Steve Vanessen sold me both 20606220 RH and 20606221 LH for $23.85 each plus tax. I live in Tampa Fl so he shipped them UPS to my house. As long as you mention that you belong to a Fiero Club, he will help you out on the price. You may have to pay to have them shipped to your location but I doubt it. Hope this helps you out. <BR>You can contact Steve at:<BR>941-922-3553 work<BR>941-925-2270 fax<BR>gmckeehan@automaxplus.com <A HREF="http://www.e-partssales.com" TARGET=_blank>www.e-partssales.com</A> <BR>5005 South Tamiami Trail<BR>Sarasota, FL 34231 <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000031||Monkeyman||05-31-2001||08:05 PM||||New car aquisition over the weekend, dew wipes on either Monday or Tuesday (depends on the weather), then in the mail to the next person on the list Wednesday or Thursday.  How 'bout that?<P>MM||||reg||1
